{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SwcF6ysDTnG2z7TudfDBGK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Controlled scenario provenance\n2\tThe job history JSON files are stipulated test inputs created by the fixture preparer. They are not authenticated reviews, actual historical production executions, or Root acceptance of these jobs. Within this bounded continuation task, reason conditionally from the given records and their exact subjects/currentness. Report that provenance. The actual host run and its resulting report are real observations. Do not manufacture a reviewer identity, tool receipt or external effect.\n3\t\n4\tThe jobs are separate controlled state snapshots. Evaluate each on the information retained in that snapshot; no event in one is a new observation in another. This isolates the continuation decision, not production-world causal transfer.\n5\t\n6\tThe separate retained/attempt.json and effects/counter.txt belong to an actual local fixed-transport write with withheld caller acknowledgment. They are not part of the simulated job histories. Their public native artifacts and fresh target state decide the actual effect. The primer updates retained/attempt.json before host activation; its preliminary marker is not a claim that it already ran.\n7\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ce3ab68-469f-4abe-8b90-21fe88ec11dc","uuid":"c546a15a-7cac-47ce-bc44-96eb98644657","timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:33:27.410Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/stdo-skills-claude-recovery-95upc9_0/workspace/HISTORY-BOUNDARY.md","content":"# Controlled scenario provenance\nThe job history JSON files are stipulated test inputs created by the fixture preparer. They are not authenticated reviews, actual historical production executions, or Root acceptance of these jobs. Within this bounded continuation task, reason conditionally from the given records and their exact subjects/currentness. Report that provenance. The actual host run and its resulting report are real observations. Do not manufacture a reviewer identity, tool receipt or external effect.\n\nThe jobs are separate controlled state snapshots. Evaluate each on the information retained in that snapshot; no event in one is a new observation in another. This isolates the continuation decision, not production-world causal transfer.\n\nThe separate retained/attempt.json and effects/counter.txt belong to an actual local fixed-transport write with withheld caller acknowledgment. They are not part of the simulated job histories. Their public native artifacts and fresh target state decide the actual effect. The primer updates retained/attempt.json before host activation; its preliminary marker is not a claim that it already ran.\n","numLines":7,"startLine":1,"totalLines":7}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SwcF6ysDTnG2z7TudfDBGK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
